  "solution": {
    "text": "Total number of ways without any restriction <math><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>!</mo></math><br />Considering two of the particular boys sit together and then assuming them as one, the total no. of ways <math><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>!</mo></math><br />They them selves can be arranged in <math><mn>2</mn></math> ways.<br />So, the required number of ways<br /><math><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>!</mo></math>",
